 "synopsis": "NLC India Renewables (NIRL), a wholly owned subsidiary of Central Public Sector Enterprise NLC India, has filed its DRHP with SEBI for an Initial Public Offering. The proposed IPO comprises a fresh issue of equity shares aggregating up to INR 3,300 crore and an offer for sale of up to 10 crore equity shares by the promoter selling shareholder, NLC India. NIRL plans to utilize INR 2,475 crore from the net proceeds of the fresh issue towards repayment or pre-payment of certain outstanding borrowings. The company may also consider a pre-IPO placement of equity shares aggregating up to INR 660 crore. NIRL develops, owns, and operates renewable energy plants.",
